{"id":59684,"ord":62,"n_segments":178,"prev":59683,"next":59685,"doc":{"id":"68515","title":"68515_Budd Johnson oral history interview","collection":"rutgers","inst":"Rutgers — Institute of Jazz Studies","interviewee":"Budd Johnson","interviewer":"","date":"","year":"","source_url":"https://rucore.libraries.rutgers.edu/rutgers-lib/68515/","url":"https://semlab.io/linked-jazz-transcripts/?t=68515"},"chapter":"Chicago, Villa Venice and Louis Armstrong","title":"The Villa Venice band lineup","category":"band_or_employer","summary":"Budd names the men in the Villa Venice band with Keg, Eddie Mallory and others.","period":"1933","year_from":1933,"year_to":1933,"words":137,"start":[86,14],"end":[87,16],"url":"https://semlab.io/linked-jazz-transcripts/?t=68515#s59684","tags":{"places":[{"name":"Europe","focus":0,"type":"region"}],"venues":[{"name":"Villa Venice","focus":1,"city":null}],"bands":[]},"people":[{"name":"Les Coyle","qid":null,"n":6},{"name":"Keg Johnson","qid":"Q1737791","n":2},{"name":"Budd Johnson","qid":"Q349082","n":1},{"name":"Bill Wilson","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Eddie Mallory","qid":"Q29824276","n":1},{"name":"Earl Mass Malsa","qid":null,"n":1}],"story":{"theme":33,"theme_name":"Chicago: the jazz migration and its clubs","community":59,"community_name":"Going north: working the Chicago jazz scene","core":false},"blocks":[{"p":86,"b":14,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"MR. JOHNSON: -- Bill Wilson and my brother --"},{"p":87,"b":0,"s":"MR.","x":": Keg Johnson."},{"p":87,"b":1,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"-- Keg Johnson, Eddie Mallory, and --"},{"p":87,"b":2,"s":"MR.","x":": What's the guitar player that comes out here? Les Mitch (Coyle)."},{"p":87,"b":3,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Les (Coyle). And what was the violin player's name?"},{"p":87,"b":4,"s":"MR.","x":": Levy, was it Levy?"},{"p":87,"b":5,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"No, I'll think of him, but he just come back from Europe."},{"p":87,"b":6,"s":"MR.","x":": But Les (Coyle) was --"},{"p":87,"b":7,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Les (Coyle) played the guitar --"},{"p":87,"b":8,"s":"MR.","x":": -- on the guitar."},{"p":87,"b":9,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"-- played a little violin too, didn't he?"},{"p":87,"b":10,"s":"MR.","x":": Little violin also."},{"p":87,"b":11,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"And anyway --"},{"p":87,"b":12,"s":"MR.","x":": Still with us in 1975."},{"p":87,"b":13,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"And Earl Mass Malsa on drums."},{"p":87,"b":14,"s":"MR.","x":": Right. You know, you guys had the best band in town."},{"p":87,"b":15,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Oh, we could cut all of that music, man. I mean --"},{"p":87,"b":16,"s":"MR.","x":": Yeah, high class, I mean that was a high class show."}]}